@@ -1536,3 +1536,46 @@ only `size`.
 - One JSON shape covers movie/show/season/episode; parse the field table in §2 with all-optional semantics.
 - Every image through `/photo/:/transcode` at exact card size; never raw `thumb`.
 - Direct play = `Media[].Part[].key` + token; server supports byte ranges.
+
+
+## Bounded remote queue reads (client policy)
+
+`plex::remote::ReadSession` reuses one already-authorized `Client`; it does not
+select a server, create a PMS PlayQueue, start playback or change saved profiles.
+A worker keeps the same session through section selection and subsequent reads.
+Its caller deadline and a 35-second ceiling cover the whole transaction; each
+HTTP operation receives at most eight seconds of the remaining time. The total
+response-body budget is 8 MiB across all requests. Cancellation and the captured
+client/token/grant generations are checked before and after each request and
+before a parsed result is returned. Cancellation does not interrupt an already
+running transport call; that call retains the finite allowance above.
+
+The section directory is read once from `/library/sections`, consistent with the
+existing whole-directory operation. At most 1000 unique string section IDs are
+accepted; a contradictory count/offset rejects the result. Item lists use
+`/library/sections/{id}/all` with `type=1` for movie libraries or `type=4` for show
+libraries, preserving PMS order. Windows are built by `paging::paged_path` and
+request at most 200 rows. Counts preserve absence: supplied values must be exact
+nonnegative integers, counts and offsets must match the returned page, and any
+later supplied total must agree with the earlier one. Repeated IDs, premature
+empty pages and malformed rows reject the collection.
+
+Library playback returns at most 500 items. Without truncation permission,
+overflow fails. With permission, `truncated` is true only after an actual unique,
+compatible 501st item is observed; a claimed larger total alone is insufficient.
+The first 500 retain full metadata, including `Media/Part`. The lookahead proves
+an omitted item and is never returned for playback. At exactly 500, a known
+matching total completes the collection; an unknown total requires an empty
+lookahead request.
+
+Explicit queue metadata uses `/library/metadata/{ids}` in chunks whose paths
+are at most 2048 bytes. IDs remain positive decimal strings of up to 20 digits;
+they are never narrowed to `i64`. Requests deduplicate IDs, while the caller
+restores duplicate occurrences in its original order. Every requested ID must
+have exactly one returned movie/episode record with a usable first `Media/Part`,
+matching the remote queue's default-version policy. Safe query parameters on a
+relative part key are preserved; credential query injection and traversal are
+rejected. The existing playback resolver remains responsible for transport,
+codec/version selection and final admission on the captured server. These are
+client-side limits and validation rules, not additional claims of live PMS or
+television validation.
